{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789175336956,"sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_8pZTLYGOr6TT1ADrKTulkJYu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git status --short"},"output":"(no output)","metadata":{"output":"(no output)","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git status --short","time":{"start":1789175336935,"end":1789175336954}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d9e66b1b54a6dd6016aa4a6289f1c87d1a4add048f0f1b1ee"}},"id":"prt_093290fd6001x6hPPg2oYNfFwW","sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","messageID":"msg_09328f8b1001cTNCKnX1UeWTfT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789175336956,"sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_oqpNcehuUD49k32Qd5mTf9WY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo"},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo</path>\n<type>directory</type>\n<entries>\n.git/\n.gitignore\n.handwork/\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nREADME.md\nsrc/\ntests/\n\n(8 entries)\n</entries>","metadata":{"preview":".git/\n.gitignore\n.handwork/\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nREADME.md\nsrc/\ntests/","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"directory","path":"/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo","entries":[".git/",".gitignore",".handwork/","package-lock.json","package.json","README.md","src/","tests/"],"offset":1,"totalEntries":8,"truncated":false}},"title":"","time":{"start":1789175336951,"end":1789175336955}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d9e66b1b54a6dd6016aa4a6289f2487d187243d19dee37697"}},"id":"prt_093290fd8001IFnLWH3EX7etWX","sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","messageID":"msg_09328f8b1001cTNCKnX1UeWTfT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789175422190,"sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_Q7hL49PWtfgw2fxG9b2DAwyD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Trace project isolation paths","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Inspect repository project reads/updates/list authorization and caching for reported organization isolation bugs. Read only, no changes. Return relevant files, root causes, suggested minimal fix, and test commands. Thoroughness medium."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f6cd6f032ffeEf2pgxsgMF039t\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Findings\n\nConfirmed **three bugs** affecting project authorization and caching. Inspection was read-only; reproduction requests modified only disposable in-memory fixtures. No files were changed.\n\n### 1. Cross-organization project reads and updates are allowed — high severity\n\n**Relevant files**\n- [src/services/project-service.ts:10–13,24–28](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L10)\n- [src/routes/projects.ts:10–12](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/routes/projects.ts#L10)\n- [src/auth/membership.ts:4–5](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/auth/membership.ts#L4)\n\n**Root cause:** `detail(userId, projectId)` ignores `userId` and returns any existing project. `update()` calls this function as its apparent authorization gate, so it also lacks organization authorization. Routes require a valid session, but authentication alone is insufficient.\n\n**Reproduced:** Bob, who belongs only to `org-b`, receives `200` for both reading and renaming `org-a`’s project `a1`.\n\n**Minimal fix:** After finding the project and preserving the existing `404` handling, call:\n```ts\nrequireMembership(db, userId, project.organizationId);\n```\nIn `update()`, retain the authorized project returned by `detail()` for cache invalidation. Always use its stored ownership—not a query/body organization ID. Keep authorization before validation, writes, and cache deletion.\n\n### 2. List cache keys collide across organizations — high severity\n\n**Relevant files**\n- [src/cache/keys.ts:2–3](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/cache/keys.ts#L2)\n- [src/services/project-service.ts:17–22](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L17)\n\n**Root cause:** `projectListKey()` accepts `organizationId` but omits it from the key. Requests with identical pagination/sort options share cached results across organizations.\n\n**Reproduction:** Warm `org-a`’s list as Alice, then request `org-b`’s list as Bob with the same options. Bob’s authorization for `org-b` succeeds, but the cache supplies `org-a`’s results.\n\n**Minimal fix:** Include an unambiguously encoded organization component and all existing list options. For example:\n```ts\nconst prefix = `projects:list:${JSON.stringify(organizationId)}:`;\nreturn `${prefix}${options.page}:${options.pageSize}:${options.sort}:${options.direction}`;\n```\nCentralize that prefix helper for both key generation and invalidation. Encoding and exact delimiters matter because organization IDs are opaque and may contain punctuation or share prefixes.\n\n### 3. Successful updates leave cached lists stale — medium severity\n\n**Relevant files**\n- [src/services/project-service.ts:24–29](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L24)\n- [src/cache/project-cache.ts:1–16](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/cache/project-cache.ts#L1)\n- [src/db/project-repository.ts:6–19](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/src/db/project-repository.ts#L6)\n\n**Root cause:** Updates delete only `projectDetailKey(projectId)`, although the current detail path does not cache anything. Cached lists are snapshots and remain unchanged after database updates. Both names and `updatedAt` affect ordering, so stale results can affect multiple pages.\n\n**Minimal fix:** After a successful authorized update, iterate `cache.keys()` and delete **every list variant for the actual owning organization**, using the exact encoded prefix above. Preserve unrelated organizations’ entries and keep list caching enabled. Existing detail-key deletion can remain.\n\n## What is already correct\n\n- List authorization runs **before cache lookup**, so current membership is checked even on cache hits. Preserve this ordering.\n- Repository list queries filter by organization; the cross-organization list leak originates in cache key construction.\n- Updates persist only `name` and the derived `updatedAt`; body ownership fields cannot reassign a project.\n- Membership checks read current membership state rather than cached authorization.\n\nThese requirements are explicitly documented in [README.md:11–21](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/README.md#L11).\n\n## Tests and commands\n\n**Executed:** `npm test` on Node `v24.21.0`: **8 passed, 0 failed**. The existing [tests/projects.test.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/2-1-opencode/repo/tests/projects.test.ts) covers happy paths, anonymous access, and invalid names, but not these isolation/cache cases.\n\nAdd regression coverage for:\n- Cross-organization GET/PATCH returning exactly `403 {error:\"forbidden\"}`, without writes or cache mutations.\n- Authorization based on stored ownership despite forged organization IDs in query/body.\n- Organization-isolated list caches, including a user belonging to both organizations.\n- Revocation taking effect immediately for GET, PATCH, and warmed list caches.\n- Update invalidation across pages, page sizes, sort fields, and directions, while unrelated organization caches remain hits.\n- Organization IDs sharing prefixes or containing punctuation.\n- Repeated identical authorized lists avoiding another repository list query.\n\nRun from the repository root:\n```sh\n# Full suite; Node >=24\nnpm test\n\n# Project-focused suite\nnode --test tests/projects.test.ts\n```\n\nThe minimal production fix is concentrated in **`project-service.ts` and `cache/keys.ts`**, with regression tests in **`tests/projects.test.ts`**.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","sessionId":"ses_f6cd6f032ffeEf2pgxsgMF039t","model":{"modelID":"gpt-6-astra","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Trace project isolation paths","time":{"start":1789175336910,"end":1789175422186}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d9e66b1b54a6dd6016aa4a6289f1087d19f98434cd88e4595"}},"id":"prt_093290fca001WUcFWUfpyAq9uh","sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","messageID":"msg_09328f8b1001cTNCKnX1UeWTfT"}}
