{"type":"text","timestamp":1789175521101,"sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","part":{"id":"prt_0932bc6ca001WV2TlzWOt8ZA3q","messageID":"msg_0932bc0ca00112WiuxdaGLFwa4","sessionID":"ses_f6cd72c6effeXppzTJW3q652tO","type":"text","text":"Implemented the organization-isolation fixes.\n\n- **Authorization:** Project reads and updates now require membership in the project’s stored owning organization. Unauthorized updates are rejected before storage or cache mutations. List membership checks remain before cache lookup.\n- **Cache isolation:** List keys now include an unambiguously encoded organization ID while retaining page, page size, sort, and direction.\n- **Invalidation:** Successful updates invalidate every cached list variant for the owning organization, leaving unrelated organizations’ cached lists usable. Caching remains enabled.\n- **Compatibility:** Existing API signatures, response shapes, and status-code conventions are preserved.\n\nAdded `tests/project-isolation.test.ts` covering unauthorized access, membership revocation, organization switching, forged ownership fields, all pagination/sorting variants, and preservation of unrelated cache hits.\n\n**Verification**\n- `npm test`: **11 passed, 0 failed**, including all 8 existing tests.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Existing tests were not modified; no dependencies were installed.","time":{"start":1789175514826,"end":1789175521100},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0054df784d2e70f0016aa4a6dad3e887d188b94d614a1f0e63","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
